  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the proved unique-common-root descent for two-prime generation and the existing expansion-range spread for mixed nonmembership. Adapt the root-cycle proof through the literal coefficient embedding to remove its unnecessary algebraically-closed base requirement. Joint induction uses only proper-divisor data; native relative degrees and existing coefficient transport finish the actual field, without an abstract certificate.",
  "discharged": "For every nonzero N, the actual rational divisor field equals Q(j,j_N). Its degree over Q(j) is dedekindPsi(N), and coefficient transport gives that same internal j-coordinate degree over every characteristic-zero coefficient field. The expanded minimal polynomial equals the primitive triangular conjugate product. A joint strong induction discharges all generation, degree, conjugate-product and nonmembership premises: unique common roots give two-prime generation, actual mixed fields identify the prime-power spread tower, coprime nonmembership supplies the first step, and native tower multiplication closes every level.",
  "remaining": "Modular ramification at 0 and 1728 and unramifiedness elsewhere, elliptic and cusp fiber counts, numerical genus, analytic realization, and the period/arithmetic/symmetric-power gates remain required. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
